{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1399235-let-s-talk-freeholds","id":1399235,"title":"Let's talk Freeholds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-27T02:26:01-07:00","id":1399235,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Let's talk Freeholds","content":"So the Book of Freeholds is interesting, it has fun contributions but it is often unclear or contradictory of other material, like how Nunnehi have Lodges instead of Freeholds, but the book says they only have access to Glades. One can assume to resolve the contradiction Lodges are just cultivated Glades, that use the Nunnehi model rather then the Balefire route.<br /> <br /> Wasn't their something about Freeholds having something like a feature like Treasures tied to them that give you half the cost but they are built into the freehold, I remember the example given being a bell that Chicaneries the Freehold hidden, but I couldn't find it in the books, closest being the Freehold Cantrip rules where you can spend double on the Cantrips rating as a Freehold power. Oh never mind I found it was the Maggies Pub Freehold in the Corebook in the Freehold section.<br /> <br /> One of the things that made little sense is it seems to imply you need the Freehold's rating in Glamour invested, well Permanent Glamour. The Corebook says you need permanent Glamour up to the rating of the Freehold invested to create the Freehold, but the Freehold Book says you need this every time new owners seize the Freehold. I guess it could be the explanation of you don't need to spend permanent Glamour build the freehold just use the starting flame or build a flame, but to attune to it you need to make permanent investment of Glamour.<br /> <br /> With the Freehold opening up the background to be a superbackground that goes past five, I am wondering should you have the invested Glamour only equal its balefire rating?<br /> <br /> And that Signet of the Flame Treasure seems, does it really justify as being Level 3? They have that Freehold Power that produces Embers for this, but you need to buy the treasure separately... what is the point? Why would you need that power? It can't be only Freeholds with this power can make Signet can it? Or only these freeholds maybe can make multiple Signets?<br /> <br /> And how did King David own two beefy Freeholds, It would seem messed up if he sacrificed Chimera or treasures to do it. Do you think he just has a bunch of Co-signers who serve him so he only invested one Glamour each?<br /> <br /> I assume Motley members can undertake the Demesnes Oath to join ruling a Freehold after its initial seizing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just re skimmed the sections because I read the Countless Dreams book and UFO are their version of Freeholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T20:13:31-07:00","id":1399481,"title":"","content":"The Noble I have who's &quot;Lucky&quot; enough to have an area where there's alot of potential Freeholds.. but not many freeholders has started the capture and fight of chimera as part of the &quot;Rites&quot; of starting to build a Freehold. Its full on Old school Roman style. The Great beasts are given every chance to win and if they do.. well they can keep the area! IF a hero wants to claim it.. well look there's a sacrifice ready!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T18:15:17-07:00","id":1399711,"title":"","content":"So, I am probably going to work on journaling/responding to several challenges and triumphs I have faced in the process of getting a &quot;24/7&quot; server up and running, but the most notable thing I have noticed with the Book of Freeholds is the fact that it lends itself more to a small collaborative form of troupe-based session-roleplay, but it lacks a lot of hard quantitative details when it to stuff like 'how to raise Balefire from level 1 to level 2' or 'what do Resources or Size actually 'do'?&quot;<br /> <br /> As a result, I have been working on expanding the crunch of Book of Freeholds to be more 'systematic' so to speak, in a manner that Freeholders (and by proxy, the regents/vassals they have) can designate Resources/Dreamstuff into upgrading the Freehold in question.<br /> <br /> I am currently working on a 20x2^(current level) cost. That is, raising a feature from 0-&gt;1 points would cost 20 Dross. Raising from 4-&gt;5 points would cost 320 dross. Once the Dross is allocated towards the improvement, it will take a number of weeks=the new level+the previous level for it to become available; it is assumed there are no 'rolls' involved as the entire Freehold and outlying Kinain and Boggans are busy pitching into the project.<br /> <br /> The Glamour/dross ratios for Balefire were tweaked for the 24/7 format for ease of bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> Many of the backgrounds (Contacts, Dreamesrs, Mentor, Resources, Retinue, Title, etc) were modified to be called &quot;Leveraged Backgrounds.&quot; This basically means that for each dot you have, you get 2 points, and you can leverage 'up to half' those points (or your dots worth) of such backgrounds to add bonus dice to assorted rolls. E.x. &quot;Leverage Contacts&quot; for bonuses to Streetwise rolls to procure black market goods, etc.<br /> <br /> The Resource feature of a Freehold was converted to act as a 'floating' resource for topping off the Leveraged Backgrounds of players able to access them.<br /> <br /> The Size feature was modified to mean two different things: First is the Balefire could not exceed the Size feature by more than 1. Basically, larger Balefires mean larger Freeholds.<br /> <br /> The second thing Size did was it dictated how many &quot;Subholds&quot; that a Freehold could have. Essentially, you can have &quot;the main&quot; Freehold, and then you can tack on secondary structures to it. Think a sprawling castle with a library wing, barracks, etc. Combine this with the reworked nature of the Resources feature, and this could also mean stuff like Resources&lt;Dreamers&gt; to represent having a recording studio, Resources&lt;Retinue&gt; for a tavern where you could hire Kinain mercenaries, etc.<br /> <br /> It's still a work in progress, but the beauty of Discord is there are quite a few bots out there to automate a lot of the datatracking, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}